#align(center)[Year 7 · Language Arts]

#tip[
  Use the *simple past* for finished actions at a specific time ("I _visited_ Paris *in 2019*").
  Use the *present perfect* for experiences or actions connected to now ("I _have visited_ Paris *twice*").
]

== Exercise 1 — Choose the correct form

Circle the correct option.

+ I (*saw* / *have seen*) that film last weekend.
+ She (*lived* / *has lived*) here since 2015.
+ We (*didn't finish* / *haven't finished*) our homework yet.
+ They (*went* / *have gone*) to the museum yesterday.
+ (*Did you ever eat* / *Have you ever eaten*) sushi?

== Exercise 2 — Complete the sentences

Put the verb in brackets into the correct tense.

+ My grandparents #blank (move) to the coast in 1998.
+ "#blank you #blank (finish) the book yet?"
+ Tom #blank (break) his arm twice so far.
+ When I was young, I #blank (not / like) vegetables.
+ It #blank (rain) every day this week.

